        "body": "The forex market runs around the clock in four sessions that follow the financial capitals of the world: Sydney (Asia-Pacific), Tokyo (Asia), London (Europe) and New York (North America). When one session closes another opens, which is why the market never fully stops.\n\nEach session favours certain currencies. Sydney is dominated by the Australian and New Zealand dollars. Tokyo is the home of the Japanese Yen, the Australian Dollar and the Chinese Yuan. London is the biggest session by volume and drives the Euro, the British Pound and the Swiss Franc. New York drives the US Dollar, the Canadian Dollar and USD/MXN. About half of all world forex volume passes through London, which is why it is the heart of the market.\n\nThe best window for beginners is the London/New York overlap between roughly 3pm and 6pm Kenyan time, when both sessions are open. This is when volatility is highest, trends are cleanest and spreads are tightest. The worst times are around midnight Kenyan time when only Sydney is trading, spreads widen and price moves slowly in unpredictable ways.\n\n- Four sessions - Sydney, Tokyo, London, New York - cover the full trading day.\n- London is the largest session; it sets the tone for the Euro and the Pound.\n- The London/New York overlap gives the cleanest moves and tightest spreads.\n- Trade pairs from their home session for the best behaviour.\n- Avoid the dead hours, the last Friday before holidays, and major news spikes until you know them."
