        "body": "A demo account gives you the exact same trading platform and the same price feeds as live trading, but with virtual money. It is where every skill you build in this academy should first be demonstrated. There is no limit to the account size or the number of accounts, which makes it the cheapest teacher you will ever have: a place to test a strategy across hundreds of trades without risking a shilling.\n\nThe beginner mistake is treating demo as \"fake\" and rushing to live. The opposite is true: you should not trade live until you have three things proven on demo - a strategy with a positive edge kept over at least 30-50 trades, the discipline to follow the rules every single trade, and journaled results you can actually review. Most newly funded live accounts die because the trader changed nothing but the urgency when real money appeared.\n\nLive trading changes you psychologically in ways demo cannot fully simulate. Real losses trigger fear, greed and revenge trading, and these emotions arrive exactly when you have no automatic habit to lean on. The solution is to bring your habit to live, not your reaction: trade the same size rules, the same journal, the same review routine, and start with the smallest live account your broker allows.\n\n- Demo uses real prices but virtual money; use it until results are consistent.\n- Prove the strategy for 30-50 journaled trades before going live.\n- Demo does not teach you fear; expect emotions to appear when money is real.\n- Keep the live starter account small and follow the exact same routine.\n- Going live early is the most expensive mistake a beginner can make."
