        "body": "Everything in this module exists to be fused into one repeatable machine: a trade setup with rules so clear that a hundred traders would take the same trade on the same chart. Start with the conditions described as a checklist. Example: (1) the 4-hour trend is clearly up (higher highs and higher lows, price above the 50 EMA); (2) price has pulled back into a zone that previously acted as resistance and turned support; (3) a bullish candlestick has closed above that zone; (4) the 15-minute chart shows no immediate counter-setup. Every box must tick or the setup does not exist.\n\nThen fix the execution in numbers before touching the platform. Entry: the market order on the confirming candle close (or a limit at the zone). Stop: below the structure that invalidates the idea - the recent swing low or the far edge of the zone - not a round pip number. Target: the next resistance level or a minimum 1:2 risk-reward. Position size: 1% of the account divided as the risk rule requires, computed once and never adjusted by mood. The whole trade, from idea to plan, takes seconds once you have internalised the checklist.\n\nFinally, run the setup like a scientist. Trade it on demo or paper for at least 20-30 iterations and journal every one before judging it at all. Track win rate, average winner, average loser and the maximum losing streak. A 45% win rate with 1:2 risk reward can be brilliantly profitable; a 60% win rate with 1:0.5 breaks even after costs. The numbers in the journal are the only honest judge of the setup, and they cannot contradict a properly kept journal. This is the difference between having an idea and having a system.\n\n- Define the setup as a checklist that must all tick.\n- Fix entry, stop, target and size in numbers before the trade.\n- Stop beyond invalidation; target from structure or a 1:2 minimum.\n- Judge the setup only after 20-30 journaled trades.\n- Win rate and risk-reward together decide profitability; journal tracks both."
